  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,1)$ is $(-1,3)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [1,4)$ is $\\{1\\}$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-1,3)\\cup \\{1\\}=(-1,3),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n-1<f(x)<3.\n$$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-1$ and $y=3$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use \"less than\" $(<)$ instead of \"less than or equal to\" $(\\le )$ at these endpoints.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
